<%#
  views/editor/articleReview.ejs

  The editor's review page for one article: who wrote it, its status, whether it is
  live, the editor's note if it was returned, the content and the publish history
  (every approval, with its date and editor).

  The content part depends on the article:
  - never published: the submitted content;
  - live with an update in progress: "Currently live" and "Submitted changes" side by
    side, with the changed fields marked (requirements: the editor must understand
    what is published now and what new content awaits approval);
  - live with no update: the live version only.

  The whole page is rendered on the server; no script is needed to read it.

  Security: only an editor ever receives this page (requireRole('editor') in
  routes/pageRoutes/editorPageRoutes.js). Everything a reporter typed (title, summary,
  body, note) is printed with the escaping tag (equals sign), so it is shown as text and
  can't run as script on the editor's page. The tag with a minus sign (no escaping) is
  used only to include our own templates (head, header, nav, partials).

  When the workflow allows a decision (only for an article awaiting approval), the
  page also shows "Approve and publish" and "Return for corrections" with a required
  note. Every article also has an Edit form (the editor can edit all articles): it
  changes the working copy, and for a live article with no update in progress, saving
  publishes the edit at once (see editArticleDraft in the controller). public/js/editor/articleReview.js sends them to the editor API with
  apiClient (every page's browser code lives in public/js/<area>/).

  Rendered by: controllers/editorController.js (showArticleReview), for GET /editor/articles/:id.
  Locals: title (the page title), review (prepared by toReviewView() in the controller)
  and categories (Article.CATEGORIES, for the Edit form).
  Includes: the shared head, header and footer, the editor nav and partials/articleContent.
  Owner: SM.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<%- include('../partials/head', { title: title }) %>

<body class="page-container">
  <%- include('../partials/header') %>
  <%- include('partials/editorNav', { activePage: 'dashboard' }) %>

  <main class="main-content">
    <p><a href="/editor">&larr; All articles</a></p>

    <article id="article-review" data-article-id="<%= review.id %>">
      <header>
        <h2><%= review.title %></h2>
        <p>
          <span class="status-badge status-<%= review.status %>"><%= review.statusLabel %></span>
          By <%= review.reporterName %> &middot;
          <%= review.isLive ? 'Live on the site' : 'Not published yet' %> &middot;
          Last change <%= review.updatedAt %>
        </p>
        <%#
          Only for an article readers can see: an article that was never published has
          no views yet. encodeURIComponent keeps the id inside the query value, whatever it holds.
        %>
        <% if (review.isLive) { %>
          <p><a href="/editor/analytics?article=<%= encodeURIComponent(review.id) %>">See its views over time (Impact Analytics)</a></p>
        <% } %>
      </header>

      <%# The note the editor wrote when returning it; the reporter sees the same note on their dashboard. %>
      <% if (review.editorNote) { %>
        <section class="card">
          <h3>Note to the reporter</h3>
          <p><%= review.editorNote %></p>
        </section>
      <% } %>

      <% if (!review.isLive) { %>
        <%- include('partials/articleContent', { heading: 'Submitted content', content: review.draft }) %>

      <% } else if (review.changedFields.length === 0) { %>
        <%- include('partials/articleContent', { heading: 'Live version (no changes in progress)', content: review.published }) %>

      <% } else { %>
        <p class="card"><strong>Changed in this update:</strong> <%= review.changedFieldLabels.join(', ') %></p>
        <%#
          Two columns side by side: the live version on the left, the submitted one on
          the right, so the editor reads them line by line. two-column is the shared class
          in public/css/main.css (SH): a Flexbox row of two columns that becomes one column on a
          phone, where the columns would be too narrow to read (requirements: responsive).
          Each included partial is one section element, so it is one column (one flex item) by itself.
        %>
        <div class="two-column">
          <%- include('partials/articleContent', { heading: 'Currently live', content: review.published, changedFields: review.changedFields }) %>
          <%- include('partials/articleContent', { heading: 'Submitted changes', content: review.draft, changedFields: review.changedFields }) %>
        </div>
      <% } %>

      <%#
        The editor's own edit (requirements: the editor can edit every article). What saving
        does depends on the status, and the summary line says it: for a live article with no
        update in progress it publishes at once (data-publishes-on-save makes the script ask
        for confirmation); otherwise only the working copy changes and the status stays.
        details/summary is plain HTML that folds the form away until the editor opens it,
        without any script. The limits (maxlength, required, the category list)
        match the server's checks, but they are only a quick answer in the browser: the
        server checks everything again, because a request can be sent without this page.
        The values are printed with the escaping tag, so a title like "<b>" fills the field
        as text.
      %>
      <% if (review.canEdit) { %>
        <details class="card" id="edit-section">
          <% if (review.editPublishesOnSave) { %>
            <summary><strong>Edit the live article</strong> (saving publishes your changes to readers at once)</summary>
          <% } else { %>
            <summary><strong>Edit the working version</strong> (the status stays "<%= review.statusLabel %>")</summary>
          <% } %>
          <form id="edit-form" data-publishes-on-save="<%= review.editPublishesOnSave ? 'true' : 'false' %>">
            <label for="edit-title">Title</label>
            <input type="text" id="edit-title" name="title" class="form-field" maxlength="200" required value="<%= review.editableDraft.title %>">

            <label for="edit-summary">Summary</label>
            <textarea id="edit-summary" name="summary" class="form-field" rows="3" maxlength="500" required><%= review.editableDraft.summary %></textarea>

            <label for="edit-category">Category</label>
            <select id="edit-category" name="category" class="form-field" required>
              <option value="">Choose a category</option>
              <% categories.forEach(function (category) { %>
                <option value="<%= category %>"<% if (category === review.editableDraft.category) { %> selected<% } %>><%= category %></option>
              <% }); %>
            </select>

            <label for="edit-image">Main image address (optional, http:// or https://)</label>
            <input type="url" id="edit-image" name="imageUrl" class="form-field" maxlength="2000" value="<%= review.editableDraft.imageUrl %>">

            <label for="edit-body">Body (leave an empty line between paragraphs)</label>
            <textarea id="edit-body" name="body" class="form-field" rows="14" maxlength="50000" required><%= review.editableDraft.body %></textarea>

            <p id="edit-message" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary"><%= review.editPublishesOnSave ? 'Save and publish' : 'Save changes' %></button>
          </form>
        </details>
      <% } %>

      <%#
        The decision buttons appear only when canTransition allows them (pending).
        The server checks again when they are used, so hiding them is only for
        clarity, never the protection.
      %>
      <% if (review.canApprove || review.canReturn) { %>
        <section class="card" id="review-decision">
          <h3>Your decision</h3>
          <p id="decision-message" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>

          <% if (review.canApprove) { %>
            <button type="button" id="approve-button" class="btn btn-primary">Approve and publish</button>
          <% } %>

          <%#
            required and maxlength="2000" give a quick answer in the browser; the server
            checks the same rules again (an empty note gets 400), because a request can
            be sent without this page.
          %>
          <% if (review.canReturn) { %>
            <form id="return-form">
              <label for="return-note">Note to the reporter: what needs to be fixed? (required)</label>
              <textarea id="return-note" name="note" class="form-field" rows="4" maxlength="2000" required></textarea>
              <button type="submit" class="btn btn-danger">Return for corrections</button>
            </form>
          <% } %>
        </section>
      <% } else { %>
        <p class="card">No decision is needed now: this article is "<%= review.statusLabel %>".
          The editor decides only on articles awaiting approval.</p>
      <% } %>

      <section class="card">
        <h3>Publish history</h3>
        <% if (review.publishHistory.length === 0) { %>
          <p class="empty-state">Never published.</p>
        <% } else { %>
          <%# reversed: the list is newest first, so the numbers count down and the first approval keeps number 1. %>
          <ol reversed>
            <% review.publishHistory.forEach(function (publishEvent) { %>
              <li>Published <%= publishEvent.publishedAt %> by <%= publishEvent.editorName %></li>
            <% }); %>
          </ol>
        <% } %>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>

  <%- include('../partials/footer') %>

  <%# apiClient first: public/js/editor/articleReview.js uses it. %>
  <script src="/js/shared/apiClient.js"></script>
  <script src="/js/editor/articleReview.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
